## Verification protocol (HITL)

Three-tier classifier ordered by *epistemic role of the datum*, not by
publisher identity. Canonical scheme in `report/inputs/verification_methods.tex`
§`sec:verif-filter` — that section is the source of record; this table is
the implementer's quick reference.

| Tier | Rule | Action |
|------|------|--------|
| 1 | Publisher *is* the producer of the datum (gov.vn / moit.gov.vn / chinhphu.vn / EVN / PetroVietnam / operator press releases / IFI project docs: WB, ADB, IEA, UNDP) | AUTO-OK + tagged primary |
| 2 | URL appears in one of four oracles: (a) `docs/pipeline.ods` References sheet; (b) `data/rag_corpus/`; (c) Zotero library; (d) domain allowlist `{gem.wiki, enerdata.net}` | AUTO-OK + tagged secondary-curated |
| 3 | Tertiary aggregation (Wikipedia, `power-technology.com`, `nsenergybusiness.com`, `reccessary.com`) or uncited | **DEFAULT-EXCLUDE.** Operator may promote per-URL by explicit decision. |

Edge cases (strictest-reading defaults; refine if they bite):

- Same domain, different role: `banktrack.org` own research → Tier 1;
  banktrack.org policy brief aggregating GEM → Tier 3. Per-URL, not per-domain.
- State news outlet reporting on a derivative doc → Tier 3 (the outlet
  is not the producer; it's reporting on someone who is).
- Dead URL whose doc is in Zotero with PDF attachment → Tier 2 (Zotero
  copy is citation of record).
- Tier 1 publisher with dead link, not in any oracle → Tier 1 if
  publisher identity is confirmable; else Tier 3 (default-excluded).

Implementation:

- Fuzzy URL+title canonicalization (host normalization `en./www./m.`,
  strip query/fragment, fuse PDF/HTML twins, fuzzy title match for
  preprint/publication pairs) — one row per *document of record*, not
  per URL string.
- Tier-2 oracle precedence: `pipeline.ods` → `rag_corpus/` → Zotero
  (API, memory `reference_zotero.md`, user ID 95318) → domain allowlist.
- Tier-1 publisher allowlist: starts small (`gov.vn`, `chinhphu.vn`,
  `moit.gov.vn`, `evn.com.vn`, `pvn.vn`, `worldbank.org`, `adb.org`,
  `iea.org`, `undp.org`, …); grows by explicit promotion.
- Tier-2 domain allowlist: `{gem.wiki, enerdata.net}`; grows by explicit
  promotion only (never by default — generics like `worldpowerdata.com`,
  `database.earth`, `worldpowerplants.com` stay Tier 3 until earned).
- Tier-3 default-exclude UX: operator sees a summary "N URLs excluded
  by default; review? [y/N]" — drill-down on demand, not per-URL prompt.
  Promotion question (per URL when drilled): "Is this URL the source of
  record for the claim, or is it citing another source?" Most tertiaries
  cite nothing → answer is trivial → exclusion maintained.
- Output: `experiments/exp3/verified_bibliography.csv` —
  `(source_url_canonical, tier, primary, oracle_hit, notes)`.

## Reconstruction strategies (compared)

| # | Strategy | Mechanics |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | **Null control** | Exp 2's unverified table, no reconstruction |
| 1 | **Batch RAG** | All verified sources in system context, one shot |
| 2 | **Incremental chronological** | One doc per turn, publication-date order |
| 3 | **Incremental random** | One doc per turn, random order (seeded) |
| 4 | **Incremental ranked** | One doc per turn, mistral-embed cosine similarity to task statement |

State for strategies 2–4: the **working report** (table + bibliography
+ per-cell provenance), a structured object. At each turn, model
receives (current report, next doc) and produces (updated report). The
model does not get a growing raw-context window — only the structured
state.

## Matrix

- Models: 5 reconstruction models (post-0134 regimes-scatter lineup).
- Strategies: 5 conditions (1 null + 4 ways).
- Reps: **3 per cell** (matches MoE rule; sufficient given Exp 1
  stability).
- Cost: reported, not controlled. Incremental strategies will be more
  expensive than batch RAG due to per-turn state replay.

## Ranker

**`mistral-embed` + cosine similarity**, fixed across all reconstruction
models. Cheap (~$0.10/M tokens; sub-cent for the whole bibliography),
deterministic, no cross-model confound. Mistral does not ship a
dedicated cross-encoder reranker (as of cutoff Jan 2026); embeddings +
cosine is the in-stack equivalent.

## Quality readout

Two figures (locked in design dialogue 2026-05-21):

1. **`fig_reconstruction_strategies.pdf`** — cost vs F1 per (model,
   strategy). Replaces retired `fig_regimes_scatter.pdf`. Family
   colouring per PR #375 / 0194 pattern; median + whiskers per Exp 1
   convention.
2. **`tab_reconstruction_quality_dims.{tex|md}`** — F1 + Coverage +
   Trade-off + Local (the four H1–H4 dimensions where measurable) per
   (model, strategy). The stateful reconstruction exposes per-cell
   provenance, so these dimensions are nearly free at scoring time.
   Lands in an Annex.

